# Mutation plan for the local-mode (unix socket) API: the transport, the session, and the
# six route+method pairs it lands.
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/local-mode.plan
#
# The decisions a reader could plausibly get wrong, in three groups.
#
# **The session.** `APILocal` installs `model.Session{Local: true}` and nothing else, and
# `IsUnrestricted()` is that one field — so `local: false` silently refuses everything and a
# fabricated `user_id` silently becomes an identity in audit records. Both are caught by
# `local::tests`, which is the only place either can be seen.
#
# **The socket.** Skipping `os.RemoveAll` means a crashed server never restarts; a mode wider
# than 0600 hands an unauthenticated, unrestricted API to every account on the host. Those two
# lines are the whole access-control story of this router.
#
# **`server_busy`.** Its parameter has four rejections that produce one indistinguishable body,
# its idle answer is a zero `time.Time` rendered two different ways, and its permission check runs
# **before** the parameter is read — an order that leaks to an unauthorised caller whether their
# value would have been accepted.
#
# The last two lines are the no-op controls and must SURVIVE.

